  "The index has exactly one discontinuity: the 12-stock average was replaced by the 20-stock average when the NYSE reopened on 12 Dec 1914, and the 1916 revision was applied retroactively to that date but not before it. Chaining straight through it puts 1896-1913 on the wrong basis, low by a constant 0.7326 (measured across 8 anchor years, stdev 0.00003). Those years are divided by that factor to put the whole line on the basis every published 'Dow since 1896' chart uses.",
